{"title":"👻 Ghost Tour: The Exhibition Grounds 🎡","startsAt":"2026-10-22T18:30:00-04:00","endsAt":"2026-10-22T20:30:00-04:00","status":"ACTIVE","type":"PHYSICAL","description":"# 👻 Ghost Tour: The Exhibition Grounds 🎡\n\n### Toronto's Haunted Fairgrounds, Dark History & One Building I Don't Like Being Near\n\nThe Exhibition Grounds have spent more than a century hosting crowds, celebrations, soldiers, shows, and some of Toronto's biggest events.\nBut underneath all that history is a darker side.\n\nThe Exhibition Grounds are said to be **one of the most haunted places in Toronto** — and I'll be honest: **this is the one place on my ghost walks that genuinely scares me.**\n\nThere's something about the atmosphere here.\nSome buildings have an energy that feels different. And when you know what happened in them, it's hard not to look at them a little differently.\n\nOn this evening ghost walk, we'll explore the grounds and hear stories of **soldiers, settlers, performers, animals, tragedies, and people who may never have completely left.**\n\nThis isn't just about trying to scare you.\nIt's about discovering the strange history hiding underneath one of Toronto's most familiar landmarks.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 What We'll Explore\n\nWe'll begin outside **Medieval Times** and make our way across the Exhibition Grounds toward the Princes' Gates.\nAlong the way, we'll hear stories connected to:\n\n* 🏚️ **The General Service Building**\n* 💀 **The Stanley Barracks** — the building that genuinely creeps me out\n* 🐎 **The Horse Palace**\n* 🏠 **Scadding Cabin**\n* 👻 Other strange stories, unexplained encounters, and haunted corners of the grounds\n\nWe'll finish at the **Princes' Gates**.\nWe'll keep a steady walking pace and **will not be entering any of the buildings**.\n\n***\n\n## 🕯️ Why This One Is Different\n\nI've done a lot of ghost walks around Toronto.\n**This is the one that actually makes me uncomfortable.**\nMaybe it's the history. Maybe it's the buildings. Maybe it's simply knowing what happened here and then standing there after dark.\n\nWhatever it is, the Exhibition Grounds have always felt different to me.\n\nSo come prepared for some genuinely creepy stories — and maybe a few moments where we all wonder whether we should really be standing there. 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** In front of **Medieval Times**\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **6:30 PM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes**.\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🚶‍♂️ **Pace:** Steady walking pace\n🏁 **End Point:** **Princes' Gates**\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$10 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis is a **curated ghost-walking experience**, rather than one of our regular social walks. The route, stories, and history have been researched and brought together specifically for this experience.\nThe fee helps support the time and work that goes into creating these walks.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🧥 Weather-appropriate clothing\n💧 Water\n📱 Your phone for photos\nAnd maybe… don't wander off by yourself. 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis experience is great for:\n\n* 👻 People who love ghost stories\n* 🏙️ Anyone fascinated by Toronto's darker history\n* 🕯️ Fans of the strange and unexplained\n* 🎡 People who want to see the Exhibition Grounds differently\n* 🚶 Anyone looking for something unusual to do on an evening out\n* 😈 People who like being scared — at least a little\n\nYou don't have to believe in ghosts.\n**You just have to be willing to walk into the dark with us.**\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the history.**\n**Stay for the ghost stories.**\n**And try not to look too closely at the buildings.** 👻","venue":{"name":"Medieval Times Dinner & Tournament","address":"10 dufferin Street, Toronto","lat":43.632648,"lng":-79.425529,"city":"Toronto"},"fee":{"amount":10,"currency":"CAD"},"group":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!","image":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/3/a/c/9/highres_535755049.jpeg"}